# This repository holds PSS source files and nothing else. There is nothing to
# build, so there are no build products to ignore.
#
# Deliberately NOT the GitHub Python template that was here initially. That
# template ignores directories by name -- `lib/`, `build/`, `dist/`, `var/`,
# `parts/`, `env/`, `target/`, `instance/`, `sdist/`, `wheels/` and, the one
# that matters here, `cover/`. "Cover" is ordinary PSS vocabulary: a `cover/`
# bucket for coverage constructs is a natural thing to add, and it would have
# been silently dropped on `git add` with no error and no output.
#
# So: ignore only things that are never corpus content, and never ignore a
# bare directory name. Check any addition with
#
#     git check-ignore -v curated/<name>/x.pss
#
# which must print nothing for every bucket name anyone might reasonably use.

# Editor and OS droppings
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# Python bytecode, in case a helper script is ever added here
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
